PURPOSE Specify the paper's nonlinear split-route master P2 over a selected pool
    as an optional reference solve, separate from the linearized RMP controller.
REFERENCES Paper Eqs. 18--21; GeneratingMasterProblemQ.cs.
NOTES This binary P2 solve uses physical-vehicle ownership and validates the
    resulting plan. Its solver bound applies to the selected route pool.
INPUT split route pool, vehicle capacities, node restrictions, input and config.
OUTPUT feasible physical plan if found; objective and bound scoped to this pool.

PROCEDURE SolveQuadraticPool(pool,capacity,node,input,config)
    Validate the same d[q,r],g[l,k],d[l,r],b coefficients as BuildSplitMaster.
    Remove routes forbidden by node; create binary x[l],x[q].
    One x[q] selects the complete package path, including both stored fragments.
    objective := etaK*SUM_l c_l*x[l] + etaR*SUM_q c_q*x[q].
    FOR every parent order r: add SUM_q d[q,r]*x[q] = 1.
    FOR every physical vehicle k: add SUM_l g[l,k]*x[l] = 1.
    FOR every current vehicle route l and complete supported transition
        loadProduct := SUM_r (
            SUM_q b[q,matching package endpoints and times]*d[q,r]*x[q])
            * d[l,r]*x[l].
        add loadProduct <= capacity[owner(l)]
             * b[l,matching vehicle endpoints and times]*x[l].
    Preserve the paper's state matching, unserved penalties and unused routes.
    Enable nonconvex quadratic solving when required by the chosen solver.
    Optimize within config.limits.referenceMaster.
    Record solverStatus, objective bound and incumbent availability separately.
    IF no incumbent exists
        RETURN QuadraticResult{status,scope=restricted_P2_pool,plan=none}.
    Check all binary, coverage, ownership and nonlinear-capacity residuals.
    plan := ReconstructPlan(pool,x,input,config).
    IF ValidatePlan(plan,input,config) fails: RETURN invalid_reference_solution.
    RETURN QuadraticResult{status,plan,physicalCost=plan.cost,objective,bound,
        scope=restricted_P2_pool,routePoolSignature,branchSignature}.

PROCEDURE CompareBinaryPoolModels(pool,capacity,node,input,config)
    linearized := SolveIntegerPool(pool,capacity,node,input,config).
    nonlinear := SolveQuadraticPool(pool,capacity,node,input,config).
    IF either solve is unfinished: RETURN comparison_open with both statuses.
    Compare feasible plans and objectives under identical route/cost/branch inputs.
    If both are solved globally, their binary-pool optimum should agree within
        tolerance because the three w inequalities enforce the product exactly.
    RETURN agreement or coefficient/solver discrepancy with evidence.

TERMINATION
    A solver bound applies to the restricted route pool, not the full decomposition.
    A validated integer feasible plan can improve the decomposition incumbent.
    Control uses the current solution and its validated objective.
